================================================================================
R6 - an impossible read range returned ok:true and one line
================================================================================
shamsu/tools/agent_tools.py - _refuse_impossible_range()

The defect, from F:\Work\demo2\test2 session 20260822-183305-4975:

    read_file(player.js, start_line=145, end_line=20)
      ok          : True
      message     : Read file.
      content     : '145|   getBoundingBox() {'
      end_line    : 145        <- silently rewritten from 20
      truncated   : True

`end = min(total_lines, max(end, start))` made every malformed range legal.
8 of 47 ranged reads in that session carried end_line < start_line; all 8 came
back as one line and a success. That exact payload went out FIVE times. Two
turns ended on "I stopped after 24 steps without finishing", and 47 of the
session's 90 tool results were reads.

After:
    {'start_line': 145, 'end_line': 20}   ok=False
       end_line (20) is before start_line (145), so that range is empty and
       player.js was NOT read. end_line is a line NUMBER, not a count. For the
       20 lines starting at 145, call read_file with start_line=145 and
       end_line=164.
    {'start_line': 200, 'end_line': 210}  ok=False   (past EOF - was ok:true,
                                                      empty content)
    {'start_line': 145, 'end_line': 165}  ok=True    (unchanged)
    {'start_line': 148, 'end_line': 153}  ok=True    (unchanged)

Second silent failure closed with it: start_line past EOF made
`lines[start-1:end]` an empty list, which came back as a successful read with
no content at all.

