SECOND BATCH - R7, R4, R3 (same day, evening)
================================================================================

R7 - reasoning clipped on screen and discarded on disk
  shamsu/action_ledger/ledger.py  - log_model_thinking now writes the trace at
      EVERY log level, bounded by MAX_REASONING_ARTIFACT_CHARS (64k).
  shamsu/cli/turn_render.py       - MAX_REASONING_CHARS 400 -> 1400, and _clip
      now cuts at a sentence/line/word boundary via _cut_at_a_boundary().

  *** A POLICY CHANGE, NOT A STALE TEST ***
  test_essential_log_level_keeps_previews_and_writes_no_model_artifacts failed,
  and it was RIGHT to: it encodes a deliberate rule that at `essential` level no
  model text reaches disk. R7 narrows that rule rather than fixing a bug in it.

  The argument for narrowing: `essential` exists to keep VOLUME down. A prompt
  is 15KB+, a response can be larger, a reasoning trace is 200-4000 chars. The
  trace is also the only artifact that cannot be reconstructed from anything
  else, and it is what you need when a session gets stuck. Live 2026-08-23 the
  ledger held `thinking_chars: 2543, cot_path: ""` while the screen clipped the
  same trace at 400 chars - the user saw "Let me: 1. Delete ..." and could not
  recover the sentence naming the three source files about to be deleted.
  Redaction is unchanged (test_secrets_are_redacted_in_prompt_and_cot_artifacts).

  The test is now split in two so the narrowed rule is explicit and reversible:
    test_essential_log_level_keeps_previews_and_writes_no_prompt_or_response
    test_reasoning_is_the_one_artifact_kept_at_every_log_level
  If that trade is not wanted, reverting is one `if self.full_artifacts:`.

R4 - no wall-clock budget on a turn
  DEFAULT_TURN_BUDGET_SECONDS = 1200, turn_budget_seconds(), checked between
  rounds in _run_turn. SHAMSU_TURN_BUDGET_S overrides; 0 disables.
  Checked BETWEEN rounds, never on the call: cancelling a generation mid-flight
  loses the work it was doing. Round 0 always runs, so a turn can never report
  a timeout without having called the model once.

R3 - the empty turn after every tool result (158 of 1385, ~9% of run time)
  A thought-with-no-answer that directly follows a TOOL RESULT is now re-asked
  once with `think: False` instead of being nudged. Same cost in calls, nothing
  added to history, and the prompt is byte-identical so the KV prefix is reused.

  *** MY FIRST ATTEMPT WAS WRONG AND A TEST CAUGHT IT ***
  I made the retry a per-ROUND flag. The retry `continue`s, which starts a new
  iteration and resets the flag - so a model that kept thinking without
  answering would have spent every round on silent retries and never been
  nudged. That is the original failure reintroduced one level up. It is now a
  per-TURN budget, MAX_SILENT_RETRIES = 2, matching MAX_EMPTY_NUDGES.
  Pinned by test_the_retry_budget_is_per_turn_not_per_round.

